Apple Silicon (Linux 6.18)
==========================

This target builds an ARM64 kernel with 16 KiB pages, the mainline Apple
SoC drivers and the Apple device trees included in Linux 6.18. The previous
6.1 default is recorded as KERNEL_TESTING_PATCHVER.

The EFI images use an existing, compatible Asahi m1n1/U-Boot environment.
GRUB uses the device tree supplied by that firmware: it must retain the
runtime memory reservations, hardware identity and firmware information
added by m1n1. Do not replace it with an unmodified build-time DTB.

The combined image is a boot/root filesystem payload for external media.
It is not an Apple internal-disk installer and does not install or update
m1n1, U-Boot, the Apple boot policy, or paired vendor firmware. Its EFI
loader is installed at the removable-media path EFI/BOOT/BOOTAA64.EFI.
Keep the existing Asahi System ESP and its vendor firmware intact.

Only features supplied by mainline Linux 6.18 are enabled; building this
target does not establish full Asahi hardware support, Wi-Fi, GPU, audio,
USB-C/Thunderbolt, or physical boot acceptance.

Platform boot and firmware references:
https://asahilinux.org/docs/platform/quirks/
https://asahilinux.org/docs/platform/open-os-interop/
